{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/2026-07-06-factory-light-test-italy-food-famous-places-and-history/audio/main-8063f369ca4f.mp3","durationSec":178.944,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":4.08,"text":"Italian food is famous around the world, but in Italy food is often local."},{"start":4.84,"end":7.46,"text":"A dish can belong strongly to one city or region."},{"start":8.2,"end":10.14,"text":"Pizza is closely connected with Naples."},{"start":11.1,"end":15.08,"text":"UNESCO lists the skill of Neapolitan pizza makers as important culture."},{"start":15.78,"end":19.06,"text":"This means people protect it as a food tradition from the past."},{"start":19.9,"end":22.36,"text":"Pasta also changes from place to place."},{"start":23.08,"end":27.34,"text":"Different regions use different shapes, sauces, cheeses, and local ingredients."},{"start":28.38,"end":30.64,"text":"Gelato is another famous food word."},{"start":31.22,"end":35.82,"text":"Good gelato is usually softer than hard ice cream, so the flavor is easy to taste."},{"start":36.54,"end":39,"text":"The useful question is not only about national food."},{"start":39.58,"end":43.74,"text":"A stronger food question asks what is local in this city or region."},{"start":45.2,"end":46.58,"text":"Rome is the capital of Italy."},{"start":47.18,"end":51.26,"text":"It is also a city where modern life and ancient history stand close together."},{"start":51.8,"end":56.44,"text":"A normal walk can pass a cafe, a busy street, and a very old stone wall."},{"start":56.44,"end":59.12,"text":"The Colosseum is one of the clearest examples."},{"start":59.78,"end":62.64,"text":"It was a large Roman amphitheater for public events."},{"start":63.26,"end":68.84,"text":"It shows that ancient Rome built huge public places, and some of them are still part of the city."},{"start":69.52,"end":73.14,"text":"The Roman Forum was once a center of public life in ancient Rome."},{"start":73.9,"end":78.8,"text":"The Pantheon is also famous because its large dome still shows Roman building skill."},{"start":79.72,"end":83.06,"text":"Rome teaches a simple world fact: history is not only in books."},{"start":83.06,"end":85.56,"text":"In some cities, history is in the streets."},{"start":85.56,"end":87.5,"text":"Venice tells a water story."},{"start":88.06,"end":91.32,"text":"It was built in a lagoon, with canals, bridges, and boats."},{"start":91.94,"end":93.44,"text":"Water shapes movement in the city."},{"start":93.98,"end":100.32,"text":"Places like the Grand Canal and the Rialto Bridge help visitors understand why Venice feels different."},{"start":101.28,"end":102.6,"text":"Florence tells an art story."},{"start":103.26,"end":109.54,"text":"It is closely connected with the Renaissance, a time when art, science, building, and learning grew in new ways."},{"start":109.54,"end":115.62,"text":"The city is famous for places like the Cathedral of Santa Maria del Fiore and the Uffizi Galleries."},{"start":116.48,"end":120.46,"text":"Venice and Florence are both Italian, but they do not teach the same thing."},{"start":121.24,"end":123.98,"text":"Venice teaches water, trade, and city movement."},{"start":124.82,"end":127.98,"text":"Florence teaches art, ideas, and Renaissance buildings."},{"start":128.88,"end":130.46,"text":"This is why real place names matter."},{"start":131.02,"end":133.9,"text":"They help learners understand the world more clearly in English."},{"start":134.72,"end":136.58,"text":"Italy looks like a long boot on the map."},{"start":137.1,"end":140.94,"text":"This shape matters because the sea is close to many parts of the country."},{"start":140.94,"end":145.88,"text":"Italy also has the Alps in the north and the Apennine Mountains running down the country."},{"start":146.6,"end":149.28,"text":"Because the land changes, local life changes too."},{"start":149.86,"end":152.16,"text":"The north has mountain areas and business cities."},{"start":153.2,"end":156.22,"text":"Central Italy has hill towns, farms, and famous art cities."},{"start":156.8,"end":160.02,"text":"The south has warm coastlines and strong food traditions."},{"start":160.02,"end":164.12,"text":"Sicily and Sardinia are large islands with their own local stories."},{"start":164.68,"end":167.98,"text":"Italy's long history also changes from place to place."},{"start":168.46,"end":178.42,"text":"Ancient Rome, Venice as a sea city, Florence in the Renaissance, Naples and food culture, and the islands all show different parts of the country."}],"words":[{"text":"Italian","start":0,"end":0.48},{"text":"food","start":0.48,"end":0.82},{"text":"is","start":0.82,"end":1.04},{"text":"famous","start":1.04,"end":1.3},{"text":"around","start":1.3,"end":1.64},{"text":"the","start":1.64,"end":1.78},{"text":"world","start":1.78,"end":2.08},{"text":"but","start":2.32,"end":2.38},{"text":"in","start":2.38,"end":2.5},{"text":"Italy","start":2.5,"end":2.84},{"text":"food","start":2.98,"end":3.2},{"text":"is","start":3.2,"end":3.38},{"text":"often","start":3.38,"end":3.72},{"text":"local","start":3.72,"end":4.08},{"text":"A","start":4.84,"end":4.94},{"text":"dish","start":4.94,"end":5.14},{"text":"can","start":5.14,"end":5.38},{"text":"belong","start":5.38,"end":5.68},{"text":"strongly","start":5.68,"end":6.12},{"text":"to","start":6.12,"end":6.46},{"text":"one","start":6.46,"end":6.66},{"text":"city","start":6.66,"end":6.9},{"text":"or","start":6.9,"end":7.1},{"text":"region","start":7.1,"end":7.46},{"text":"Pizza","start":8.2,"end":8.48},{"text":"is","start":8.48,"end":8.8},{"text":"closely","start":8.8,"end":9.22},{"text":"connected","start":9.22,"end":9.58},{"text":"with","start":9.58,"end":9.84},{"text":"Naples","start":9.84,"end":10.14},{"text":"UNESCO","start":11.1,"end":11.44},{"text":"lists","start":11.44,"end":11.84},{"text":"the","start":11.84,"end":12.08},{"text":"skill","start":12.08,"end":12.38},{"text":"of","start":12.38,"end":12.58},{"text":"Neapolitan","start":12.58,"